Ladybird puts a text decoration line’s top edge on a device pixel, fills
solid and double lines as rectangles, and draws a thin dotted line with
square dots, as the other engines do. Blink snaps the decoration rect in
SnapYAxis() and fills solid and double lines with DrawLineAsRect(), with
the second line of a double one a thickness plus 1 away, which Ladybird
keeps. Gecko snaps its rect in GetTextDecorationRectInternal() and, in
PaintDecorationLine(), dashes a dotted line of 2 device pixels or less
with square dots and a thicker one with round ones. WebKit snaps its
line bounds in computeLineBoundsAndAntialiasingModeForText().
